    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d906-a2">

                <pb facs="1078" n="982" sameAs="frus:frus1898/pg982"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2.—Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hay to Mr.
                            Day.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1898-06-25"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">June 25,
                    1898</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Had an interview with Lord Salisbury. The convention of 1888 guarantees free
                    navigation of Suez Canal to ships of all powers, belligerent or otherwise. Lord
                    Salisbury thinks it improbable that any power should object, as there will be no
                    ground for objection, if we should send war ships through the canal. I send by
                    mail copy of convention.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hay.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
